 "overview": {
  "id": "PR_kwDOUcx-yc8AAAABHkAYhw",
  "number": 106,
  "title": "fix(app): keep a file's header in view when it collapses",
  "url": "https://github.com/antfu/pulls.review/pull/106",
  "body": "## Why\r\n\r\n- Marking a large file as reviewed collapses it while the viewer sits deep inside it.\r\n- The page then lands several files further down, so files get skipped without notice.\r\n\r\n## What\r\n\r\n- Collapsing a file pins its header back under the page header when its start is above the viewport.\r\n- The next file follows directly below the collapsed header.\r\n- A file whose start is still in view keeps the current scroll.\r\n- This covers the reviewed checkbox, the caret, and a header click.\r\n- Tests cover a file scrolled past its start and a file still in view.\r\n\r\n## Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n- Have a file with a big diff opened\r\n- Mark that file as viewed by clicking the checkbox\r\n- The file will skip other smaller files because the header drifts\r\n- You end up skipping files without realising\r\n",
  "bodyHTML": "<h2 dir=\"auto\">Why</h2>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Marking a large file as reviewed collapses it while the viewer sits deep inside it.</li>\n<li>The page then lands several files further down, so files get skipped without notice.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">What</h2>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Collapsing a file pins its header back under the page header when its start is above the viewport.</li>\n<li>The next file follows directly below the collapsed header.</li>\n<li>A file whose start is still in view keeps the current scroll.</li>\n<li>This covers the reviewed checkbox, the caret, and a header click.</li>\n<li>Tests cover a file scrolled past its start and a file still in view.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Steps to reproduce</h2>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Have a file with a big diff opened</li>\n<li>Mark that file as viewed by clicking the checkbox</li>\n<li>The file will skip other smaller files because the header drifts</li>\n<li>You end up skipping files without realising</li>\n</ul>",
